    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0503" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg407"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">638.5131/8</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May 3,
                        1926</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received May 11.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 802</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the Haitian
                    Government has addressed a note to the chargé d’affaires of the French
                    Government at Port-au-Prince, by the terms of which the Haitian Government
                    abrogates, on the 27th of July next, the Franco-Haitian Commercial Convention of
                        1907.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d233-f1"/></p>
                <p>A copy and translation of the note, together with two other notes bearing
                    thereon, are transmitted herewith for the Department’s information.<anchor
                        n="10" xml:id="d233-f2"/></p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John H. Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
